  "notes": "Saudi Kayan Petrochemical Company (Saudi Kayan; ticker 2350) audited financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/415_0_2026-03-03...). Auditor PwC. Board of Directors approved and authorized issue on 24 February 2026 (7 Ramadan 1447H). Saudi Kayan has no subsidiaries - these are standalone (not consolidated) statements, so there is no non-controlling interest. The five primary statements (printed pages 7-11) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x); the notes are digital text. Amounts are in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). FY2025 was a heavy LOSS year: Saudi Kayan reported a gross LOSS of SAR 893.9m (cost of sales exceeded revenue) and a net loss of SAR 2,293.9m (2024: net loss SAR 1,803.7m) as petrochemical prices stayed below cash cost and finance costs on its large project debt weighed; accumulated losses reached SAR 6,521.0m and total equity fell to SAR 9,179.8m. net_income, operating_income, gross_profit, comprehensive_income and FY2025 EPS (-1.53) are all negative. income_taxes_and_zakat is the single 'Zakat (expense) / benefit' line. operating_income is the reported 'Operating loss'. other_reserves combines the statutory reserve, 'Other components of equity' and the actuarial reserve (the statutory reserve of SAR 288.5m was released to accumulated losses in 2025). long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current 'Debt' and its current portion (project / Islamic financing - the group refinanced heavily in 2025, repaying SAR 7.24bn and drawing SAR 7.99bn); IFRS 16 lease liabilities are mapped separately. defined_benefit_obligation is the non-current 'Employee benefits'; employee_benefits_current is the current portion. depreciation_amortization sums depreciation of property, plant and equipment, depreciation of right-of-use assets and amortisation of intangible assets from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Additions to property, plant and equipment'. interest_paid is 'Finance cost paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'. No dividend (loss-making). The cash-flow statement reconciles with no separate foreign-exchange effect line. Statement page references are the printed page numbers: financial position 7, profit or loss and OCI 8, changes in equity 9, cash flows 10-11.",
